;; Append-only measurement series (the documented exception to "documents hold
;; current state only" -- a time series IS the value). Each entry is one run of
;; os/aiueos/scripts/os-coverage.cljs. Never rewrite an entry: a coverage number
;; that improves because someone edited history is worth nothing.
;;
;; :core is emitted/declared over :relevance :core rows. It is scoped to the
;; evidence supplied, and a zero row usually means "this profile did not
;; exercise it", not "it does not work" -- several zeros here are contradicted
;; by physical contracts (physical-kotoba-native-k16-v1.edn has
;; :arp-request-reply :passed while net-link reads 0/3, because the log that
;; proves it is not one of these logs). Raising the number therefore has two
;; honest routes and one dishonest one: feed evidence from profiles that
;; already pass, close real gaps, or widen the taxonomy denominator. The third
;; is why :declared is recorded alongside :emitted.
[{:at "2026-09-09"
  :evidence ["usb-gate-disk.out"]
  :profile :release-image-qemu-disk-boot
  :core {:emitted 29 :declared 114 :pct 25.4}
  :note "First measurement. The evidence is a single QEMU release boot, and
         that boot itself does not pass the shared UEFI suite (it stops at
         AIUEOS_VIRTIO_INPUT_FAIL, a QEMU 10.0.3 device-model difference), so
         everything after that point in the sequence is unproven here for a
         reason unrelated to AIUEOS. cluster, inference, net-link, net-stack,
         process, remote and isolation all read 0 for profile reasons rather
         than capability reasons.
         The taxonomy reported ten markers it did not know about on its first
         run and they were added; that check exists because a benchmark whose
         denominator silently stops growing flatters itself over time."}
 {:at "2026-09-09"
  :evidence ["kernel-serial.log" "uefi-debug.log" "usb-gate-disk.out"]
  :profile :uefi-suite-default-build-plus-release-image
  :core {:emitted 67 :declared 114 :pct 58.8}
  :route :a-evidence-from-a-profile-that-already-passes
  :note "25.4 to 58.8 with no capability change. The first measurement read a
         log from the USB gate, which attaches no NIC and boots the release
         image; running the shared suite directly produced 76 distinct markers
         against that log's 39. admission, memory, process and smp are 100
         percent and were never below it -- the earlier number was measuring
         the wrong boot.
         net-link and net-stack remain 0 and are still profile scope, not
         capability: no profile run so far attaches virtio-net AND reaches the
         stack. Closing them needs a network-bearing run, which is the next
         honest route (a).
         Found on the way, and larger than the number: the README claimed the
         suite fails on QEMU 10.0.3 at AIUEOS_VIRTIO_INPUT_FAIL. On exactly
         that version it emits AIUEOS_VIRTIO_INPUT_OK and finishes
         AIUEOS_UEFI_SMOKE_OK with exit 0. The gate's downgrade is the release
         IMAGE, not the host -- the build passes the suite and the release
         image does not, and the release image is what would run on a node."}
 {:at "2026-09-09"
  :evidence ["evidence-all.log" "evidence-esp-uefi.log"]
  :profile :uefi-suite-union-of-three-modes
  :core {:emitted 74 :declared 114 :pct 64.9}
  :route :a-evidence-from-profiles-that-already-pass
  :closed [:VIRTIO_NET :DHCP :IPV4 :TCP :VTD :VTD_IR :DMA_POLICY :ECDSA_PUBLIC]
  :note "58.8 to 64.9, again with no capability change, and the reason is worth
         more than the number. The suite's switches are MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE
         MODES, not additive flags: AIUEOS_ECDSA_PUBLIC_KAT makes the guest run
         that KAT instead of the full boot. And every scenario wrote to one
         reused path, so each run overwrote the last.
         Both together meant the suite proved things no surviving file showed.
         Measured: a run with AIUEOS_TEST_NET=1 and AIUEOS_TEST_DMAR=1 exited
         0, which those switches only permit when AIUEOS_DHCP_OK, AIUEOS_VTD_OK
         and AIUEOS_DMA_POLICY_OK are all present -- the gates grep for them --
         yet the file left behind held four markers from a later, shorter mode
         and none of those three. smoke-qemu-uefi.sh now appends each run's
         serial output to evidence-all.log, after the exit status is captured
         so the copy cannot clobber it.
         net-link and net-stack were profile scope exactly as suspected, and
         are no longer zero.
         CAVEAT ON THE 100 PERCENT: isolation reads 6/6 on VT-d markers
         measured under QEMU emulating Intel. The K16 is an AMD Ryzen 7 7735HS.
         That row's coverage transfers to this board not at all, and it is the
         one place where a rising number here means less rather than more.
         Next lever, untried: AIUEOS_SSH_HOSTFWD against remote 0/6."}
 {:at "2026-09-09"
  :evidence ["evidence-all.log" "evidence-esp-uefi.log"]
  :profile :uefi-suite-union-plus-amd-vi-observation
  :core {:emitted 74 :declared 114 :pct 64.9}
  :route :b-a-defect-in-the-measurement-itself
  :note "The headline did not move and the measurement got better, which is the
         only combination this ledger should ever be pleased about.
         Booting the guest behind AMD-Vi for the first time -- the K16's actual
         IOMMU class, which QEMU 10.0.3 can emulate -- showed
         AIUEOS_DMA_POLICY_OK emitted as `dmar=absent test-only-unisolated`.
         Under VT-d the same marker reads `dmar=validated dma=vtd-isolated`.
         One name, two opposite meanings, and this script counted names: it was
         crediting an explicitly unisolated boot with isolation.
         Fixed by letting the taxonomy require a payload substring for markers
         whose _OK is a report rather than a verdict. The first substring chosen
         was `isolated` and it discriminated NOTHING, because
         `test-only-unisolated` contains it -- the negative case is spelled as
         the positive with a prefix. Caught by running the control rather than
         trusting the string; `validated` separates them.
         Verified both directions: AMD-Vi-only evidence now reads isolation 3/6
         with DMA_POLICY unproven, and evidence containing a real VT-d boot
         still reads 6/6. The union stays 74/114 because it genuinely contains
         an isolated boot."}]
